[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ETH-W5500 Extension System Requirements
UID: ETH-SYS
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
System requirements of the W5500 Ethernet extension for the KM271-WiFi.
The extension is plugged onto the extension header J7 of the main board
and adds wired 10/100 Mbit/s Ethernet. Its requirements refine the main
board requirement KM271-SYS-005.

Scope: EXTENSIONS/ETH_W5500, design state in the repository (2025-09-28),
reviewed for production on 2026-11-25. Review findings are recorded as
requirements with COMPLIANCE "Not met" or "Partially met".
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Function

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-001
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Wired Ethernet for the KM271-WiFi
STATEMENT: >>>
The extension shall provide a 10BASE-T/100BASE-TX Ethernet port for the
KM271-WiFi.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-002
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Host interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The extension shall connect to the host only through the extension header J7
of the main board (SPI, interrupt, reset, power).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-022
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYA-103

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-003
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Constraint
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Firmware independence
STATEMENT: >>>
The extension shall be usable by every supported firmware with standard
drivers (ESPHome ethernet type W5500, Arduino ETH with W5500).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-004
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Link indication
STATEMENT: >>>
The extension shall indicate link and activity by LEDs at the RJ45 jack.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-023

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-005
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Could
VERIFICATION: Test
COMPLIANCE: Not verified
TITLE: Optional Power over Ethernet
STATEMENT: >>>
The extension may supply the KM271-WiFi from Power over Ethernet through an
optional PoE converter module.
<<<
COMMENT: Connector J3 for a Traco TEC2 class module; not tested.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Power

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-010
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Simulation, Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Not met
TITLE: Supply from the main board
STATEMENT: >>>
In the default assembly the extension shall be supplied from the 3.3 V rail of
the main board, so that it benefits from its step-down converter.
<<<
SOURCE: ETH review 2026-11-25 (S1)
COMMENT: >>>
JP4 (3V3 from main board) and JP5 (5 V via LDO) are both open ex works, so the
board is unpowered unless the user closes one.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-011
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-011
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Simulation, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Weak slot supply
STATEMENT: >>>
With the extension fitted the system shall still operate at a slot source
resistance of at least 2 Ohm.
<<<
SOURCE: ETH review 2026-11-25 (S1)
COMMENT: >>>
Met with JP4: W5500 supply stays above 2.97 V up to about 2.2 Ohm. With JP5
only up to about 0.9 Ohm.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-011

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Environment, mechanics and safety

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-020
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Mechanical
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Fit on the main board
STATEMENT: >>>
The extension shall fit on top of the ESP32 module of the main board inside
the KM271 slot and be fixed mechanically and isolated electrically from it
(e.g. by an adhesive pad).
<<<
SOURCE: EXTENSIONS/ETH_W5500/README.md
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-040

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-021
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Protection
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection, Analysis
COMPLIANCE: Partially met
TITLE: Galvanic isolation of the network port
STATEMENT: >>>
The network port shall be galvanically isolated from the board circuitry
according to IEEE 802.3 (1500 V rms).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Transformer is rated, but copper of the primary side is only 0.2 mm away from
line side and shield (see ETH-HW-031).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-043

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-022
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: EMC
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Review, Test
COMPLIANCE: Partially met
TITLE: EMC of the network port
STATEMENT: >>>
The extension shall not degrade the EMC of the KM271-WiFi and shall withstand
common mode surges on the network cable.
<<<
SOURCE: ETH review 2026-11-25
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-042

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Production

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-030
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Manufacturing
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Not met
TITLE: Assembly by a PCB service
STATEMENT: >>>
The extension shall be producible and SMT assembled by JLCPCB with parts in
stock at LCSC for a batch of 100 boards.
<<<
SOURCE: ETH review 2026-11-25
COMMENT: >>>
Würth RJ45 634008137521 only 47 pcs in stock; SMD alternative
HC-RJ45-5JAS-1-5-01 (C20417896) needs a footprint change.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: KM271-SYS-050

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ETH-SYS-031
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Manufacturing
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Analysis
COMPLIANCE: Not met
TITLE: Parts cost target
STATEMENT: >>>
The cost of the assembled parts per board should not exceed 4 USD at 100
boards, including the JLCPCB setup fees for extended parts and excluding the
PCB itself and the assembly service.
<<<
SOURCE: ETH review 2026-11-25
COMMENT: Current parts 10.02 USD, recommended variant 3.65 USD.

[[/SECTION]]
